<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hammer DeRoburt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1922–1992</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hammer DeRoburt was a Nauruan politician who led his country to independence and served as its first president. As Head Chief of the Nauruans he negotiated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, rejecting resettlement and securing independence on 31 January 1968 and control of the phosphate industry. He was president for most of the period from 1968 to 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hammer-deroburt.jpg" alt="Hammer DeRoburt" width="233" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dokai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hammer_DeRoburt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
